# BUG: a list of held functions cannot be written in a module file.
#
# Expected: `kanso check bugs/partial_in_list` reports ok. `&a` holds `a`
# (the book, ch05: "& supplies what you have and waits for the rest"), and a
# list of held functions is a list of values.
#
# Actual: `[&a &b]` and `. push &a` both fail with
#   error[formatting]: canonical form requires exactly one space here
# pointing at the `&` of the second element, and the parenthesised spelling
# `[(&a) (&b)]` fails with "these parentheses group nothing". No spelling of
# the list passes check, so the only way through is `[(x -> a x) (x -> b x)]`.
#
# The same `fs = [&a &b]` passes in a file run with `kanso play`, so the
# two paths disagree about the formatting rule. Each error is also printed
# twice.
fn a n
  n + 1

fn b n
  n * 2

pub fn run n
  fs[1] n + gs[1] n

fs = [&a &b]

gs = []
  . push &a
  . push &b
